<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Tae Kwang 1996 net soars.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Tae Kwang 1996 net soars.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			     26,129    vs 16,079</p>
<p>    Net					   29.09 vs     17.90</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)	 20    vs     20</p>
<p>    Turnover				 1,041.03 vs  1,046.75</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    57.26 vs     33.97</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both gain)	    7.59 vs	0.01</p>
<p>NOTE - Tae Kwang Industry Co Ltd is South Korea's leading maker of textiles and audio systems. Its share capital was unchanged at 1.11 million shares. A company official said the huge extraordinary gain came from government compensation for its use of the company's land for infrastructure construction.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
